Authority of PVTA to Enforce This Decree and to Promulgate Rules. The PVTA shall be
vested with the overall responsibility and authority of implementing and enforcing the provisions of this

Decree, and for this purpose, to time hereafter such rules and regulations or order as it may deem proper and
necessary, in addition to or supplementing the provisions of this Decree, including but not limited to such
orders or regulations.
(a) Providing for the issuance of licenses, permits, accreditations and the terms and conditions thereof, and for
the renewal, refusal, suspension or revocation of such licenses, permits and accreditations;
(b) Prescribing the fees for licenses, permits and other accreditation;
(c) Prescribing the terms and conditions of the purchase commitment and the amount of bond;
(d) Prescribing the type, location and use of trading centers;
(e) Prescribing the trading forms to be used by buyers, including the reports to be submitted by them;
(f) Prescribing the procedure for mediation and arbitration in case of controversy between the buyers and
(g) Fixing reasonable minimum prices for tobacco after taking into consideration the prevailing world market
conditions, production cost, reasonable margins of profits for the farmers, dealers, manufacturers and
exporters, the quality of the tobacco and other relevant factors and conditions;
(h) Respecting the buying, selling, advertising, handling, shipping and transporting, redrying and exporting of
tobacco by buyers, other traders or end-users;
(i) Prescribing the manner in which buyers shall sell, deliver, or transfer their purchases to redrying plants or
other buyers and end-users;
(j) Prescribing the descriptions or specifications of certain grades of tobacco, and the guidelines for
application of the official grades;
(k) Prescribing the powers, jurisdiction and duties of the PVTA tobacco inspectors or graders;
(l) Respecting the cleanliness and sanitation of tobacco to be sold or offered for sale or stored;
(m) Prescribing the areas where tobacco may be grown and/or limiting the maximum quantity of tobacco to be
produced thereon;
(n) Ordering the burning, destruction or condemnation of any standing tobacco crop that is infested with
Mosaic disease or other serious tobacco infestation;
(o) Providing for the exemption from this Decree or the regulations, or any part thereof, any person or group
(p) Respecting any matter necessary or advisable to carry out effectively the intents and purposes of this
such rules and regulations or orders that PVTA may promulgate shall, upon approval by the Office of the
President, be considered as part, and shall have the same full force and effect, of this Decree.
